The speed of the hero's movement is somewhat randomized, to make the
whack-step dance (so useful in 3.2.2) less attractive. But monsters'
movements are not randomized relatively to one another. When the hero
is surrounded by a crowd of nasties, their attacks appear synchronized,
because it is only the hero that is getting more or less movement
points.

An experiment in wizard mode: A cursed scroll of genocide created four
rust monsters. The hero (very fast due to speed boots) stood and
waited. Each time '.' was pressed, there were either 0, 8 or 16 attacks
(the R's get two attacks per move). If they were purple h's...

If the monsters' movements were randomized individually, the chance of
all of the crowd getting extra moves at the same time would be small.

Do you think the effect (which I think makes the game somewhat harder)
is a desirable one?

